{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.4924276525530277, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. Nothing in the diff reads files, pastes answers or uses test labels. The inner CV and the stacking out-of-fold loop split only the training data, by scaffold groups.", "No bug that makes the result meaningless. The eigendecomposition shortcut is correct: (K + lam*I)^-1 y = U diag(1/(s + lam)) U^T y, with mu subtracted and added back the same way as before. The final fit still uses np.linalg.solve with the chosen lam and wr.", "This is a speed change, not a modelling change. It halves the RF trees, halves the LGB rounds while doubling the learning rate, and cuts the stacking folds from 5 to 3 and the kernel-ridge inner CV folds from 4 to 3. It also narrows the kernel-ridge search: wr is fixed at 1.0 instead of searched over (0.5, 1.0, 2.0), and lam now ranges over (0.03 to 3.0). A small loss of accuracy is expected.", "Recomputed z: (0.4895 - 0.4924) / (0.0042 * sqrt(1/1 + 1/1)) \u2248 -0.49. This matches the reported -0.495; the small gap is rounding. The candidate is worse but within noise, so reject is consistent.", "The comparison rests on 1 run on each side, so it has little power. There is no evidence this is an improvement."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Cut compute (fewer trees/rounds, fewer CV folds, single kernel weight) so the stacked job fits within 10 minutes, using full-line SEARCH matches.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "walnut", "idea_id": "b051", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.4894866999475836, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.4894866999475836, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1_lipo_HH_1_cs3-crash_fix-7_1795057103275", "kind": "crash_fix", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.028666499999999998, "cost_usd_plan": 0.028666499999999998, "latency_s": 11.556923788040876, "requested_model": "sonnet", "role": "repairer"